            <ArticleTitle>New options for untreatable coronary artery disease: angiogenesis and laser revascularization.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>577-83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Some patients with severe symptomatic coronary artery disease despite maximal medical therapy are not eligible for bypass surgery or percutaneous coronary intervention, but may be eligible for two newer therapies: therapeutic angiogenesis with growth factors and transmyocardial laser revascularization.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
